Security campaign <%= @security_campaign.name %> has been opened on your repositories

<% if managers.empty? %>
<%# Rare case where there are no managers or all manager users have been deleted. %>
A new security campaign with <%= pluralize(number_with_delimiter(alerts_count), 'alert') %> for your repositories called <%= @security_campaign.name %> has been created.
<% else %>
Your campaign <%= 'manager'.pluralize(managers.size) %> <%= managers.map { |manager| manager_name(manager) }.to_sentence %> <%= 'has'.pluralize(managers.size) %> created a new security campaign with <%= pluralize(number_with_delimiter(alerts_count), 'alert') %> for your repositories called <%= @security_campaign.name %>.
<% end %>
This campaign is due on <%= @security_campaign.ends_at.strftime("%b %-d, %Y") %>.

<% enabled_repositories.each do |repository| %>
  <%= repository.name %>: <%= campaign_url_by_repository(repository:) %>
<% end %>

For more information on security campaigns read the documentation: <%= security_campaigns_help_url %>
